{
  "reading": "Iron Man is a second Shabraz trigger aimed at Shabraz; with Krang it is the 28-counter wheel, but that needs a 4-, 5- and 5-drop all resolved and alive, a T8+ board, while the deck's gap is the T6 kill (18.2%; T10 already 99.3%). Four goldfish screens find no cut where he is a clear upgrade: none improves killed by T6, and the cleanest (Willie Lumpkin) is flat on speed and damage and worse on early hands. Under the 'only clear, obvious upgrades' bar this is NO CHANGE; if the pilot wants him on his own word, the cut is Willie Lumpkin.",
  "log_entries_read": [],
  "cut_candidates": [
    {"card": "Willie Lumpkin, Postman", "why": "The only screened cut where Iron Man reads flat on killed by T6 (+0.0 pts [-0.2,+0.3]) and damage @T10 (+1.8 [-1.9,+5.5]).", "cost_of_cutting": "A 2-mana unblockable draw engine that feeds Shabraz on curve, and its 'can't attack you' rider the goldfish cannot see (no opponents); goldfish: stall +1.3 pts, hand can act by T3 -0.4 pts, extra cards by T8 -1.2.", "difficulty": "contested", "orphans_stack": []}
  ],
  "add_candidates": [
    {"card": "Iron Man, Armored Avenger", "closes": "threat-density", "source": "prompt", "why": "Pilot named it; doubles Shabraz's per-draw growth and gives counter-bearing attackers (Jaws) flying.", "natural_cut": "Willie Lumpkin, Postman"}
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    {"question": "Does the goldfish land the Iron Man + Krang + Shabraz wheel turn on the commander-damage clock (no commander-lethal row printed)?", "settled_by": "goldfish", "why_it_matters": "The card's case is that ceiling; the screens show no speed gain."}
  ],
